20260529.114844.037 [<ideas.........] [performance without comparing against previous commits, using ratio-based comparisons within the same build, and relying on]
20260529.114846.371 [<ideas.........] [median timings from repeated executions with warmup runs.]
20260529.114846.578 [<ideas.........] [Fixed fixture sizes of n=1024 and n=20 are used for lattice and random configurations. Absolute thresholds or relative]
20260529.114846.752 [<ideas.........] [ratios such as max_ratio 1.15, 2.5, and 3.0 are applied. Pytest runs in CI with wall-clock timing on shared runners, using]
20260529.114846.910 [<ideas.........] [JSON baseline files like optimizer_speed_baseline.json for reference_p95_ms. The posterior() function operates at the Python]
20260529.114847.113 [<ideas.........] [level via EpistemicNearestNeighbors wrapper. The regression test specifically compares against commit 9eaa27, ensuring]
20260529.114847.335 [<ideas.........] [detection of slowdown regardless of tie_break_neighbors setting. These approaches push assumptions to their extremes for]
20260529.114848.996 [<ideas.........] [robust testing.]
20260529.114849.155 [<ideas.........] [Consider scenarios where the system's behavior becomes undefined or extreme, such as when inputs approach mathematical]
20260529.114849.192 [<ideas.........] [limits or when algorithmic complexity grows uncontrollably. Explore alternative performance metrics beyond wall-clock time,]
20260529.114849.290 [<ideas.........] [like memory usage or cache efficiency, to detect inefficiencies that may not manifest in timing alone. Investigate methods]
20260529.114849.384 [<ideas.........] [that decouple performance evaluation from specific implementation details, focusing instead on abstract correctness]
20260529.114851.830 [<ideas.........] [properties or theoretical guarantees about the systems behavior under varying conditions.]
